.TH EUCLID-CLI-EDS-LIST-ZONES 1 "November 2026" "euclid-cli 2.3.2" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-eds-list-zones \- list the account's zones
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli eds list-zones
[\fB\-\-prefix\fR|\fB\-p\fR \fITEXT\fR]
[\fB\-\-page\-size\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB\-\-page\-index\fR \fIN\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Lists the zones of the account you are logged in to, in the namespace
your session is scoped to, ordered by name, each with how many record
sets it holds.
.PP
A zone your grants do not let you read is left out of the list, so a
principal granted one zone sees that zone. The
.I total
counts every zone in the namespace, whichever of them were listed.
.PP
Zones of other accounts are never listed, and neither is
.IR euclid.internal ,
which is made from what runs rather than stored.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-prefix " " \fITEXT\fR
Only zones whose name starts with this.
.TP
.BR \-\-page\-size " " \fIN\fR
Most zones to return. Without it, all of them.
.TP
.BR \-\-page\-index " " \fIN\fR
Zero-based page, used with
.BR \-\-page\-size .
.SH OUTPUT
A JSON object:
.I zones
\- each as
.BR euclid-cli-eds-get-zone (1)
shows it \- and
.IR total .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The zones were listed, possibly none.
.TP
.B 1
The request could not be sent or was refused.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli eds list-zones
euclid-cli eds list-zones --prefix lab. | jq -r '.zones[].name'
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-eds (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eds-get-zone (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eds-create-zone (1)
